                    <birth when="1745">
                        <placeName/>
                    </birth>
                    <death when="1827"/>
                    <occupation>OCCUPATION</occupation>
                    <note type="editorial">
                        <p>This entry has been coded to the David Davis the Elder (the father). However, Ed Pope notes: "David Davis DNB 1745-1827 poet and dissenting minister was a radical in politics and became an Arian in theology but some of his congregation broke away to form Unitarian churches. His son David Davis Dict Welsh Biog 1778-1846 was a Unitarian and the diaries of his son Timothy Davis 1779-1860 are in the Nat Libr of Wales (5487-99). As far as I can gather none of the ministries of this family were in London so they are less likely to have been any of the later Davis entries (see Davis after 1805)."</p>
                    </note>
